The rule for k_recovery says it returns the object recovered from the reply, as canonical JSON text, or NO_OBJECT. For the input fence[ A ], the reply is a fence containing only the object A, so the recovered object is A, and k_recovery returns the canonical JSON text of A. For the rewritten text fence[ A ] S, the fence now contains A and S. The recovery rule says the object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one. Since the fence holds A and S, the last object inside the fence is S, so k_recovery returns the canonical JSON text of S. Therefore the answer moves between the two texts.